  "question": {
    "text": "A rectangular frame <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCD</mi></math> made of a uniform metal wire has a straight connection between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;made of the same wire as shown in the figure.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AEFD</mi></math>&nbsp;is a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;&amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>EB</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>FC</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The entire circuit is placed in a steadily increasing uniform magnetic field directed into the plane of the paper. The rate&nbsp;of change of the magnetic field is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the resistance per unit length of the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the currents in the segments&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AE</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>EF</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>AE</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>EF</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>AE</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>EF</mi></msub></mfrac></math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0017_6ba6e127b385.jpg\" style=\"width: 193px; height: 179px;\" />"
  },
